  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 5. What happens to the iodine that gets liberated in the reaction
    between hydrogen peroxide and potassium iodide occurs?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'The liberated iodine undergoes reduction with thiosulphate ions
    to form iodide and tetrathionate ions.

    The reaction proceeds as follows:

    2(S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>)<sup>2-</sup>+
    I<sub>2</sub>-  2I<sup>-</sup>+ (S<sub>4</sub>O<sub>6</sub>)<sup>2-</sup>'
  options:
  - The liberated iodine undergoes oxidation
  - 'The liberated iodine undergoes reduction '
  - 'The liberated iodine undergoes displacement reaction '
  - 'The liberated iodine undergoes combustion '
  correctOptionIndex: 1
